<title>GERMANY: Goldman ups Allianz rating to outperformer.</title>
<headline>Goldman ups Allianz rating to outperformer.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs said on Thursday that it has upgraded German insurance group Allianz AG to &quot;market outperformer&quot; from &quot;market performer&quot;.</p>
<p>A company spokeswoman confirmed the rating change had been issued on Thursday in London.</p>
<p>Goldman's insurance analysts were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Allianz shares were up 144.50 marks at 3,049 marks in pre-bourse IBIS dealings after reaching a new record high at 3,061 marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
